# The paths whose changes make the tree "with changes" in a build stamp: git pathspecs, one per line, read by both the
# harness's tree_stamp (stamp.sh) and the build's stamp (test/benchmarks/build-stamp.gradle.kts), so an install the
# build stamped is judged by the rule it was stamped under. Blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped.
#
# The whole tree, but the reports: a --report session writes its results under results/reports/ (tracked), and a
# report, new or edited, is output, not code; no build or harness step reads it.
:/
:(top,exclude)test/benchmarks/results/reports
